hto|n|of Cut ; The act or process of making an incision, or of severing, felling, shaping, etc. ; Something cut, cut off, or cut out, as a twig or scion cut off from a stock for the purpose of grafting or of rooting as an independent plant; something cut out of a newspaper; an excavation cut through a hill or elsewhere to make a way for a railroad, canal, etc.; a cut.	a:1vs3,54,2~1vs3,54,2	n:16al,55,6;2b2h,27,1~16al,55,6;2b2h,27,1	N:nl1,49,3;18cg,24,2~nl1,49,3;18cg,24,2
